 "summaries": [
  {
   "section": "Tires",
   "text": "All tires observed were matched by brand and had tread depths of 4 and 3/32nds at the front and 5/32nds at the rear. All tires are a safety concern, dry rot, and have uneven wear."
  },
  {
   "section": "Exterior",
   "text": "Rear wiper blade worn. Rear bumper is misaligned with passenger side quarter panel. There are minor misc scratches around the vehicle. Normal for mileage and most too small to see in photos. There is a notable large ding on the rear passenger side quarter panel. Front passenger side door dent. Decals on mirror housings. Both rear quarter panel moldings are loose and misaligned. The exterior lights and washer functioned properly."
  },
  {
   "section": "Interior",
   "text": "The steering wheel shows some wear and tear as seen in pics. Normal for mileage. There is light wear to the seats. Stains were observed. The inner door panels show wear consistent with age and mileage. The interior trim shows normal wear consistent with age and mileage. TPMS light is on. The headliner shows areas of stains. Marks, and stains on sunvisor. I noted no smoke or unusual odors. The climate controls and interior electronic systems worked as designed. I noted that the windows, locks, mirrors, and gauges operated properly."
  },
  {
   "section": "Mechanical",
   "text": "Only one key fob was shown during inspection. I noted full accessible fluids and no visual leaks were observed."
  },
  {
   "section": "Road Test",
   "text": "There is a notable humming noise that does increase with speed. Possible poor dry rot condition tires, and or wheel bearings. Further diagnosis recommended. Vehicle does pull hard right when steering is placed straight. More diagnosis is needed. The tire pressure monitoring light is on. This will need further diagnosis. The engine started and ran normally. The performance of the transmission, braking, and suspension systems were good. Connected OBD scanner and found no codes."
  }
